# Pentatonic Box 5 Lick (repertoire plan: st-pent-box-5). An original 8-bar study in A minor
# pentatonic box 5, frets 2 to 5, over a one-chord Am7 groove. Four 2-bar phrases in call and
# response: phrases 1 and 3 ask (they stop on E and on G), phrases 2 and 4 answer (they come home
# to A on string 3, fret 2). All 12 notes of the box are used, and nothing else.
# One finger per fret, as the Scales screen shows the box: finger 1 on fret 2 (strings 4 and 3),
# finger 2 on fret 3 (strings 6, 5, 2, 1), finger 4 on fret 5 (every string). The hand never moves.
# The last note, A on string 3 fret 2, is held for two beats with vibrato from finger 1: rock the
# hand from the wrist so the note wavers evenly, about two waves per beat.
title: Pentatonic Box 5 Lick
composer: Sixstring Academy
